  "title": "0. Operational-level MDO in the EME (NW Scotland and the Minches)",
  "about": "Notional joint force (south-east) against an opposing force (north-west) across land, maritime, air and space, about 250 km across in a Joint Warrior-style area. Things to look for: airborne ES out-hears ground ES; radars are the loudest emitters and are fixed first; the L-band barrage loses about 19 dB against Link 16 (3 MHz hops over 255 MHz); blue's VHF net hops over 30-88 MHz (about 34 dB against a spot jammer) while red's single-channel net is denied by blue's spot jammer: the EP lesson; GNSS jamming from high ground reaches aircraft, the frigate and precision fires; blue EA denies the red VHF net. Tap any symbol to focus on it. First run takes a couple of minutes (new terrain tiles).",
